{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-202610281956554510748578268d9d6khiaEugl","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"gemini-3.5-flash","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_df0063b92c4b485d81fc2ba169b88094","name":"mcp__figma__use_figma","input":{"code":"(async () => {\n  // Let's inspect reaction property structure in Figma plugin API.\n  // The action type for navigation in Figma API is:\n  // - trigger: { type: \"ON_CLICK\" } or { type: \"AFTER_TIMEOUT\", timeout: 1500 } (since AFTER_DELAY was renamed to AFTER_TIMEOUT, or maybe is just different)\n  // - action: { type: \"NODE\", destinationId: targetId, navigation: \"NAVIGATE\", transition: { type: \"DISSOLVE\", duration: 0.3, easing: { type: \"EASE_IN_AND_OUT\" } } }\n  // Wait, let's write a script that queries one existing prototype node if possible, or checks what types are allowed.\n  // Let's test if we can check reactions schemas or just use a standard simple structure:\n  // trigger: { type: \"ON_CLICK\" }\n  // action: { type: \"NODE\", destinationId: target, navigation: \"NAVIGATE\", transition: null }\n  // Wait, the error said:\n  // - expected type to be \"BACK\" | \"CLOSE\" or similar, or \"URL\" or \"CONDITIONAL\" or \"SET_VARIABLE\"...\n  // Ah! To navigate, is type \"NODE\"?\n  // Yes! The error lists:\n  // Unrecognized key(s) in object: 'destinationId', 'navigation', 'transition' at [0].actions[0]\n  // Wait! Let's read the error details:\n  // \"Required value missing at [0].actions[0].transition.easing\" -> Oh! transition needs \"easing\"!\n  // And for trigger \"AFTER_DELAY\", it says:\n  // \"Invalid literal value, expected 'AFTER_TIMEOUT' at [0].trigger.type. Required value missing at [0].trigger.timeout.\"\n  // Beautiful! This tells us:\n  // 1. Use trigger `type: \"AFTER_TIMEOUT\", timeout: 1500` instead of `AFTER_DELAY`.\n  // 2. Use `transition: { type: \"DISSOLVE\", duration: 0.3, easing: { type: \"EASE_IN_AND_OUT\" } }` (adding `easing`).\n  // Let's run a test with just one connection to verify!\n  \n  const page = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(\"2002:2\");\n  const f01 = page.children.find(c => c.name === \"01_Splash\");\n  const f02 = page.children.find(c => c.name === \"02_Home\");\n  \n  if (!f01 || !f02) return \"Frames not found\";\n  \n  try {\n    f01.reactions = [{\n      trigger: { type: \"AFTER_TIMEOUT\", timeout: 1500 },\n      actions: [{\n        type: \"NODE\",\n        destinationId: f02.id,\n        navigation: \"NAVIGATE\",\n        transition: { type: \"DISSOLVE\", duration: 0.3, easing: { type: \"EASE_IN_AND_OUT\" } }\n      }]\n    }];\n    return \"Test connection SUCCESS!\";\n  } catch (e) {\n    return \"Test connection FAILED: \" + e.message;\n  }\n})()\n","description":"Test schema alignment for figma reactions properties.","fileKey":"pNVsMbFlqHuHgCQFsjUPkH"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":83568,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"494b4549-32cd-4fcc-b024-fd0ae7aff445","uuid":"8b4a84a5-1a6a-48e2-8642-b9678fa072a5","timestamp":"2026-10-28T19:57:10.855Z","tool_use_meta":[{"id":"call_df0063b92c4b485d81fc2ba169b88094","display_name":"Use Figma","server_display_name":"figma-authenticated-proxy","tool_name":"use_figma"}]}
